			"Message": "fix(Project): Advance 3 element submodules with Cocoon live state, Mountain IPC hardening, and Sky bridge decomposition\n\nAdvance Land/Element submodules in a coordinated round-trip spanning the extension host, native backend, and editor UI layer.\n\n**Cocoon** replaces stale/empty state placeholders with live-tracking counterparts that extensions query at runtime. `MakeUriStub` provides a minimal URI when `LazyURI.parse` fails, preventing folders from being silently dropped from the workspace list. `__visibleTextEditors` is now upserted on `didChangeTextEditorSelection` and filtered on `$acceptModelRemoved`, so GitLens/Error Lens/formatters see real open-editor state. `createTerminal` pushes into `__terminals` with proper dispose cleanup. A module-level `_AllDiagnostics` cache mirrors every `DiagnosticCollection.set/delete/clear` call, and `getDiagnostics()` returns real aggregated diagnostics with `diagnostics.didChange` event emission.\n\n**Mountain** delivers three fixesets: (1) file write handlers now update metadata and notify Cocoon of configuration changes via `configuration.change` Vine notification, so extensions' `ConfigCache` invalidates the affected key rather than serving stale data. (2) `StorageWriteDebouncer` race resolved by reordering the flush loop to take the pending item before clearing `FlushScheduled`; the workspace-scoped debouncer is now correctly selected instead of always routing through the global debouncer; low-level IPC noise (`file:open`, `file:close`, `textFile:save`) suppressed via skip list; Cocoon-connect boot latency eliminated by removing the 3-second blocking `WaitForClientConnection` from `languages:getAll`/`languages:getEncodedLanguageId` handlers. (3) Lock contention reduced in `ScanAndPopulateExtensions` by swapping an N-insert loop for a single pointer-swap, and in `DiagnosticProvider` by snapshotting under the lock then aggregating outside it.\n\n**Sky** decomposes ~2500 lines of inline handler registrations in `Bridge.ts` into four dedicated module files via dynamic imports: `InstallWebview.ts` (webview lifecycle, custom editors), `InstallEditorOperations.ts` (decorations, text edits, selections, reveal), `InstallTreeView.ts` (data provider attachment with exponential backoff retry), and `InstallUiRequests.ts` (show-message/input-box/quick-pick dialogs). Each module receives only its required dependencies through a thin injector interface, eliminating global-scope closure capture across unrelated handlers.",
			"SHA": "21c3681b99864ae1e8b02c4bdd3cf7358015edd5"
		},
