				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Advance 3 element submodules with save notifications, Undo/Redo routing fix, and IPC bridges\n\nAdvance Land/Element submodules in a coordinated update that extends the editor save lifecycle, fixes macOS keyboard routing, and adds three new Sky IPC bridges.\n\n**Mountain** fires `$acceptModelSaved` via Vine after successful disk writes in both `FileWriteNative` and `TextfileWrite`, enabling Cocoon to dispatch `onDidSaveTextDocument` to subscribed extensions (format-on-save, organize-imports, save listeners). The save is fire-and-forget (tokio::spawn) to prevent Vine IPC failures from cascading to the workbench caller. Both handlers gain `dev_log` instrumentation for write latency and byte count. On macOS, removes Undo/Redo from the native Edit submenu via `AppMenu::SetAppMenu` so Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z reach Monaco's keydown handler instead of being intercepted by AppKit's responder chain. Non-fatal; logs a warning and keeps the default menu if the override fails. No-op on Windows/Linux.\n\n**Sky** adds three bridge implementations: `InstallDiagnostics.ts` routes diagnostics from Mountain to `IMarkerService` for in-editor error visibility; `InstallScm.ts` mirrors SCM state and registers providers against the live workbench service; `InstallSearch.ts` routes file and text search queries to Mountain's handlers.\n\n**Maintain** regenerates rustdoc output against Rust nightly 1.97.0, updating static asset hashes, search index entries, crates.js, and inline source references to match the current toolchain.",
			"SHA": "c29b18affb77f31c56e100bb5d0e38f49e9126e1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
