			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Advance 14 element submodules with Mountain fixes, Air cleanup, and ecosystem maintenance\n\nPush 14 Land/Element submodules forward in a coordinated chore/fix round-trip. The headline changes are Mountain's runtime fixes and Air's dead-code removal, with the remaining updates spanning documentation regeneration, dependency bumps, license alignment, and build manifest polish.\n\n**Mountain** fixes four classes of issues: (1) shell PATH inheritance so git/Node/language servers resolve after Finder/Dock launch when `IsTty()` is false; (2) git-availability caching to prevent a transient false from the first probe (fired before PATH is extended) from permanently disabling the SCM UI; (3) removal of prematurely-introduced `prepare_call_hierarchy`/`prepare_type_hierarchy` gRPC handlers and import-path disambiguation (`Msg` aliases, qualified `MountainVinegRPCService`, `RunTime()` method call, `MetricType` alias); (4) gating `tauri_build::build()` behind `CARGO_BUILDING_DOCS` so `cargo doc` succeeds without Sky Astro assets, plus Brotli pre-bake as `beforeBundleCommand` and a `Record` bump to 1 in Info.plist.\n\n**Air** removes 98 lines of stale dead code (`ApiVersion` struct and `ApiVersionManager` left from the modularization extract) and adds `#[derive(Debug)]` to `RetryManager`, `CircuitBreaker`, `BulkheadExecutor`, and `ResilienceOrchestrator` for structured logging. A follow-up fix removes the ambiguous `pub use ApiVersion::*` re-export that shadowed the new module name.\n\n**Sky** changes `licenseName`/`licenseUrl` in `Public/product.json` from MIT to CC0-1.0, aligning editor metadata with the NLnet NGI0 Commons Fund public-domain positioning.\n\n**Grove** replaces inline `license = \"MIT\"` with `license-file = \"LICENSE\"` in Cargo.toml so the full MIT license text ships with the published crate.\n\n**Cocoon** regenerates `RouteManifest.ts` (timestamp advanced to 2026-05-20T04:19:17Z, 135 Mountain-side methods) and rebuilds Target/ artifacts with no source-level changes.\n\n**SideCar** regenerates rustdoc HTML for Rust nightly 1.97.0 (up from 1.96.0), updating CSS/JS asset hashes and const-unstable tracking annotations.\n\n**Common**, **Echo**, **Mist** advance their Documentation/Rust submodule pointers. **Common** also merges a dependabot bump for `@cloudflare/workers-types` 4.20260519.1.\n\n**Rest** syncs its submodule pointer. **Output** and **Wind** merge their Current branches with no new commits. **Maintain** advances with a clean merge commit.\n\nThis round-trip stabilizes Mountain's runtime environment and IPC handlers, eliminates dead code in Air, aligns license metadata across the project, and keeps all documentation regenerated against the latest Rust nightly.",
